OCGRAPH 1
DOMAIN pcg
NAME PG_ForestScatter
DESCRIPTION Sample PCG graph: trees on gentle ground, thinned by noise, jittered, then pruned so crowns do not overlap. Point a PCGVOLUME at it with `graph Content/PCG/PG_ForestScatter.ocgraph`; swap the mesh paths for your own. See docs/PCG.md.
# sample on a 3 m landscape lattice (world-anchored, so streamed cells agree)
NODE surface SurfaceSampler 0 0 spacing=300
PIN surface out out points
# a hash-noise density field, 40 m features
NODE noise DensityNoise 220 0 cell=4000 octaves=3
PIN noise in in points
PIN noise out out points
NODE dense DensityFilter 440 0 min=0.5
PIN dense in in points
PIN dense inside out points
PIN dense outside out points
# keep to slopes a tree can stand on
NODE slope SlopeFilter 660 0 min=0 max=30
PIN slope in in points
PIN slope inside out points
PIN slope outside out points
# break up the lattice, vary the size, spin each tree
NODE jitter TransformPoints 880 0 posMin=-120,-120,0 posMax=120,120,0 rotMin=0,0,0 rotMax=0,0,360 scaleMin=0.8,0.8,0.8 scaleMax=1.4,1.4,1.4
PIN jitter in in points
PIN jitter out out points
# denser noise wins; 4 m between trunks
NODE prune SelfPrune 1100 0 radius=400 priority=density
PIN prune in in points
PIN prune out out points
NODE trees WeightedMeshSpawner 1320 0 meshes=Meshes/Tree_Pine.ocmesh:3,Meshes/Tree_Fir.ocmesh:1
PIN trees in in points
PIN trees out out points
LINK surface.out noise.in
LINK noise.out dense.in
LINK dense.inside slope.in
LINK slope.inside jitter.in
LINK jitter.out prune.in
LINK prune.out trees.in
